&lt;p&gt;We’re seeking a curious, analytical intern who brings a fresh perspective and is eager to help the Financial Planning &amp;amp; Analysis team identify ways to improve. As a Financial Planning &amp;amp; Analysis Intern at MongoDB, you’ll build relationships across the business and serve as a trusted partner to the Product &amp;amp; Technology Finance team. You’ll develop a strong understanding of business drivers and how financial plans support MongoDB’s broader objectives.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;In this role, you’ll collaborate with stakeholders on budgeting, headcount planning, and resource optimization, while building and maintaining financial and operating models. You’ll also help improve how we input and manage forecasts in our financial systems, and conduct ad hoc analyses to inform operating strategies, resource allocation, and investment decisions for product initiatives.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What we are looking for in you:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;In the process of receiving a Bachelor’s or Master&#39;s degree in Finance, Economics, Math or a related field&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Foundational experience using data and spreadsheets to support decision-making, with curiosity about a career in financial planning and analysis.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Uses sound judgment when working with incomplete data, making and clearly explaining reasonable assumptions while knowing when to pause and seek guidance.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to balance accuracy with efficiency, knowing when to prioritize each.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proficient in Microsoft Excel, Word, and PowerPoint and Google Sheets, Docs, and Slides&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong written and verbal communication and ability to collaborate effectively via Slack and other tools&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Have a minimum of one quarter/semester remaining in university studies after the internship concludes. Graduation date in Fall 2027 or Spring 2028&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Must be authorized to work in the United States.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you&#39;ll find at MongoDB&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Authentic Culture: A workplace where you are encouraged to bring your whole self to work, we believe that Embracing the Power of Differences is the best way to broaden our own perspectives and foster innovation.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Personalized Mentorship: Pair up with a Mentor, a Program Advisor from the Early Talent Recruitment Team, and an &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.mongodb.com/careers/diversity-and-inclusion&quot;&gt;Employee Resource Group&lt;/a&gt; (ERG) Guide to foster your growth.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Career Coaching Sessions: Access to a tailored training program designed uniquely for interns’ personal and professional development.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work-Life Harmony: Embrace &quot;Bloom for Interns&quot; with access to mental and physical health benefits, paid time off, free lunch, and more!&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Impactful Projects: Contribute to projects where you can Make it Matter - your meaningful work will see the light of day.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Exclusive Networking: Attend &quot;Speaker Series&quot; and &quot;Roundtables&quot; to connect with our executives and departmental leaders.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Vibrant Community: Build connections with fellow interns and join after-work social events, virtual gatherings, and local city activities to create connections and friendships.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Relocation Support: Financial assistance, housing, and a commuting stipend to allow you to comfortably settle into your new location.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Path to Full-Time: A chance to see if MongoDB is where you see yourself long term with the possibility of receiving a full time offer at the end of the summer!&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
